  "result": "I added `clamp(cents, low, high)` to `shop/money.py`, and all 12 tests pass.\n\n```python\ndef clamp(cents: int, low: int, high: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Limit cents to low..high inclusive.\"\"\"\n    if low > high:\n        raise ValueError(f\"low > high: {low} > {high}\")\n    return max(low, min(cents, high))\n```\n\n- **Tests:** there was no test file for `money.py`, so I created `tests/test_money.py` using `unittest`, like the other test files. The `ClampTests` class checks a value inside the range, below `low`, above `high`, exactly on each limit, `low == high`, and that `low > high` raises `ValueError`.\n- **Test command:** pytest isn't installed, so I ran the command from the README: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`.\n- **Not committed.** Running the tests also created untracked `__pycache__/` folders under `shop/` and `tests/`, which you may want to add to `.gitignore`.\n\nToken Beggar: routed 1 subtask(s) to sonnet",
